@@ -0,0 +1,51 @@
+# Forge Harness
+
+Headless gRPC adapter around the Forge rules engine for the MTG combo-discovery
+research project.
+
+## Build
+
+From the Forge repository root:
+
+```bash
+~/tools/apache-maven-3.9.11/bin/mvn \
+  -pl forge-harness -am package -DskipTests
+```
+
+The shaded jar is written to:
+
+```text
+forge-harness/target/forge-harness-2.0.15-SNAPSHOT.jar
+```
+
+## Run
+
+Development assets are resolved relative to `forge-gui-desktop`, so launch from
+that directory:
+
+```bash
+cd forge-gui-desktop
+java -Djava.awt.headless=true \
+  -jar ../forge-harness/target/forge-harness-2.0.15-SNAPSHOT.jar \
+  --port 50051
+```
+
+The matching protobuf contract is maintained in both:
+
+```text
+../combo-discovery/proto/forge_env.proto
+forge-harness/src/main/proto/forge_env.proto
+```
+
+Keep these copies synchronized until the protocol is moved to a shared package.
+
+## Current Scope
+
+The harness currently supports basic game lifecycle, Forge AI/goldfish/remote
+players, priority decisions, partial state inspection, and sequence-free log
+events. `Snapshot` and `Restore` are intentionally not implemented yet.
+
+Before research-scale search, implement the protocol changes documented in
+`../combo-discovery/ARCHITECTURE.md`: game/decision IDs, independent event
+streaming, typed decisions, max-turn enforcement, complete state semantics, and
+deterministic snapshots.
