 ```
 
+`--assets <path>` pins the asset root explicitly, so the jar can be launched
+from any working directory:
+
+```bash
+java -Djava.awt.headless=true \
+  -jar /abs/path/to/forge-harness/target/forge-harness-2.0.15-SNAPSHOT.jar \
+  --assets /abs/path/to/forge-gui-desktop \
+  --port 50051
+```
+
+`<path>` may be either the assets root itself (a directory containing `res/`,
+e.g. `.../forge-gui`) or a launch/install directory whose sibling
+`../forge-gui/res` exists (e.g. `.../forge-gui-desktop`). The harness fails fast
+at startup with a clear message if neither exists.
